{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use","id":1362488,"title":"[+] What house rules do you use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-21T12:47:17-08:00","id":1362488,"title":"[+] What house rules do you use?","content":"I had the impression, that this topic was already somewhere in the forum, but now I cannot find it (If I was right, feel free to delete or merge it). <br /> <br /> Tell me about you houserules. Especially the smaller ones, one so minuscule that you wouldn't bother mentioning it in other threads. Why you introduced them? Do they fix something you find a bug or do they intentionally change the tone or scope of the game. You can list just some of them which work particularly well.<br /> <br /> This is a [+] thread, notation borrowed from another forum, so we generally simply do not criticise other's solutions. What we might do is to suggest some different modifications to the same effect. We may ask one another about the practical effects of the changes etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:53:38-08:00","id":1362489,"title":"","content":"This hasn't really come up much at all in my current game, where there's no dedicated crafters (a couple characters have some dots in it, but that's it, no charm investment), but I don't have the whole &quot;each Craft type is its own Ability&quot; thing. Instead, when you take Craft, you pick an initial area you focus in, and you can craft that easily, and other fields use your Craft dots, but are penalized based on how distant they are from your basic area of focus. Area of focus acts much like Lore backgrounds, and a crafter can learn new areas of focus at about the same difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T13:52:35-08:00","id":1362510,"title":"","content":"Crafts and Martial Arts are both not bought as new Abilities each time, but single purchases to expand your skills. I think this is a pretty common thing at least for the forums.<br /> <br /> This might be a bit more than &quot;small,&quot; but we're pretty happy with changing how Craft projects are defined. For mundane projects, we use a more narrative approach were the impact on the story is a bigger consideration. A sword could be a basic, major, or superior project based on how important that sword is. This decision defaults to the player not the ST. So if a player's making a sword and wants it to be a basic project is saying that they don't expect this to be a big deal in the plot, it's a backup weapon for another character, it's a proof of skill, a way to make some quick coins, etc. The player wanting to make a superior project sword is saying this sword is supposed to change the fate of a kingdom even if it isn't magical; it's going to draw the pleasure of a local god to bless a political marriage, be a symbol of this newly merged royal family for generations, etc. Moving it up to an extended check gives the ST chances to add complications to the process (assuming you don't switch to some of the house rules on extended actions out there). Batching items is expected. You don't make one sword per peasant you're arming into battle group, you make a batch of swords for them; the end goal of &quot;arm the new battle group,&quot; is what matters.<br /> <br /> This addresses some of the issues with the Crafting rules for us as people that generally like the framework provided.<br /> <br /> The start of a new game is considered the end of a prelude story even if you don't play one for any mechanics that reset/etc. at the end of a story instead of the start of one. It's always silly to me that players don't get to start with some random little thing because a rule was worded that way. There was a &quot;story&quot; before the game actually starts, so that sort of benefit should be available.<br /> <br /> Leaders overseeing projects have a DV of Intelligence + Bureaucracy to defend against attempts to disrupt their projects. This keeps things from being massive roll drive efforts, but it gives Bureaucracy something to do in the basic rules, and makes Exalted rule over huge swathes of Creation make more sense as they're just more resilient institutions (though you don't have to be Exalted to have a DV 5 institution like the Guild around).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T13:55:22-08:00","id":1362511,"title":"","content":"PCs can upgrade to Essence 2 at 48 exp spent instead of 50. This is to avoid the awkward limbo state where you have enough exp to raise your Essence in theory, but you can't actually spend the required 50 exp on Charms until you reach 60 exp 2 games later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T14:18:04-08:00","id":1362517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362511#post1362511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PCs can upgrade to Essence 2 at 48 exp spent instead of 50. This is to avoid the awkward limbo state where you have enough exp to raise your Essence in theory, but you can't actually spend the required 50 exp on Charms until you reach 60 exp 2 games later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like that limbo, it incentivizes PCs to spread out by picking up a 10xp Charm. It's a fun dilemma: Pick up my first E2 at 58XP at a 2XP surcharge, or skip the surcharge but have to wait until 64XP for my first E2 charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T14:25:20-08:00","id":1362518,"title":"","content":"Flat XP costs, and switching to using XP for chargen instead of BP. Scaling costs are bad design, and so is BP. Fortunately, we've known this for a while and so it was trivially easy to convert<br /> <br /> I also changed how solar XP works so that everyone has the same total. Whenever anyone meets one of the conditions, everyone gets +1 solar xp. Same 4xp cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T19:02:18-08:00","id":1362562,"title":"","content":"Does \u201cTracking whether you actually earned your Solar XP\u2019s too much of a bother and I interpret the requirements generously enough anyway that I\u2019m quietly just assuming you did\u201d count as a houserule? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T20:48:25-08:00","id":1362569,"title":"","content":"I limit Craft to 6 Abilities - if you buy that much, you're a master craftsman, nuff said. Specifically Weapons, Armor, Structures, Jewelry, Food, and Essence (Corresponding to Fire/Water/Earth/Air/Wood - and Essence). <br /> <br /> I give 2 bonus silver xp as a separate role bonus for any crafter that remembers to craft something, even if they fail all the criteria and/or the project. This is in addition to the regular bonuses (At least in my Celestial game. It hasn't come up for the Dragon-Blooded).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T23:01:36-08:00","id":1362584,"title":"","content":"Handwave training times if what they're buying is just improving stuff they use in-session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T02:07:12-08:00","id":1362598,"title":"","content":"The Burning Name (from the Pact with an Ifrit Lord initiation) has the Flame tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T02:28:37-08:00","id":1362600,"title":"","content":"Character creation works like V5, players can pick from different packages that are all worth the same amount of xp.<br /> <br /> Battle groups deal (Size + Drill) dice of damage to crashed targets instead of one-shotting the Black Claw stylist while being completely irrelevant to the guy in artifact heavy armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T15:10:24-08:00","id":1362739,"title":"","content":"When purchasing Excellencies, including with your character-creation charm picks (but not with the 5 free excellencies), Dragonbloods count Excellency cost as half normal. For starting charm picks, each one buys 2 Excellencies. I also use flat XP and replace BP with a pack of starting XP; if you have leftover starting XP you can't spend (because the flat XP costs I'm using don't have anything cost 1XP), that gets transferred over to your Solar/Lunar/Dragon/Whatever XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T16:11:50-08:00","id":1362748,"title":"","content":"The golden Rule, the orichalcum rule, and the storyteller rule are known as the abusive GM rules and are not applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T16:27:45-08:00","id":1362751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362748#post1362748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The golden Rule, the orichalcum rule, and the storyteller rule are known as the abusive GM rules and are not applied.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Leave the thread. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T02:02:05-08:00","id":1362824,"title":"","content":"Once you have bought a Craft or Martial Art, any new purchases of lower or equal dots only cost half xp rounding up.<br /> <br /> Whenever you buy a dot in any craft, you get one silver point. Buying your fifth dot in a craft gets you one gold point also. This applies at character creation as well. I suppose if anyone ever bought the craft xp to craft dots charms I'd have to revise this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T04:38:57-08:00","id":1362846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362751#post1362751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Leave the thread. </b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> In my 25 years of rpgs gaming I've never seen those rules used in any manner other than to screw over the players and railroad the story to play out exactly how the GM wants. No game I've been in has ever lasted more than 1 session after their invocation. I'm not alone I hear stories all the time about how GM arbitrarily change the rules to screw over players and force their narrative do the player's throats. I used the name specifically because GMs who crush players fun to have their own are the ones using those rules. Role playing is a hard hobby to get people to join and I've seen a lot of promising new gamers drop out because of this. It's the reason I am very selective about the groups I play with. <br /> <br /> The general rules of a game serve as the common framework for the players and GM to communicate their story with and those three rules break that understanding, communication, and trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T04:42:58-08:00","id":1362847,"title":"","content":"I think the problem was more that your solution presented (maybe inadvertently) others GM using these rules as &quot;abusive&quot;, while these rules constitute a core value of the game, developers, and a part of the community that use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T05:07:59-08:00","id":1362852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362846#post1362846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my 25 years of rpgs gaming I've never seen those rules used in any manner other than to screw over the players and railroad the story to play out exactly how the GM wants. No game I've been in has ever lasted more than 1 session after their invocation. I'm not alone I hear stories all the time about how GM arbitrarily change the rules to screw over players and force their narrative do the player's throats. I used the name specifically because GMs who crush players fun to have their own are the ones using those rules. Role playing is a hard hobby to get people to join and I've seen a lot of promising new gamers drop out because of this. It's the reason I am very selective about the groups I play with.<br /> <br /> The general rules of a game serve as the common framework for the players and GM to communicate their story with and those three rules break that understanding, communication, and trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, glad I have avoided those kinds of GMs in my 17 years of roleplaying. Rarely have I ever seen it used that way, but instead usually see it applied when niche case rules interactions cause something that seems to either break the game or make it less fun for everyone involved. Guess this largely comes down to play-style, as some groups are all on board with the &quot;collaborative storytelling&quot; experience and others seem to be locked into a GM vs players mindset.<br /> <br /> However, it is my opinion that it was a bunch of wasted word count to have three rules that all essentially say the same thing, especially when those rules are often assumed to be a given for pretty much <i>any </i>RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25108-ikeulhu","name":"ikeulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T05:19:48-08:00","id":1362856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ikeulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362852#post1362852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, glad I have avoided those kinds of GMs in my 17 years of roleplaying. Rarely have I ever seen it used that way, but instead usually see it applied when niche case rules interactions cause something that seems to either break the game or make it less fun for everyone involved. Guess this largely comes down to play-style, as some groups are all on board with the &quot;collaborative storytelling&quot; experience and others seem to be locked into a GM vs players mindset.<br /> <br /> However, it is my opinion that it was a bunch of wasted word count to have three rules that all essentially say the same thing, especially when those rules are often assumed to be a given for pretty much <i>any </i>RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I just started some DD5 with people that have very few experience in RPG and I was surprised by how much some people really want to stick to the rules, compared to my former group of friends, even in some case where they don't make sense or do not serve the story. (Just last Tuesday I had my first case of &quot;I don't want the wizard to do this so I attack him to put him unconscious&quot; since something like 10 years. The worst is when I realized I had no excellent social system like Exalted to try and solve this puzzle, so I just had to tell players &quot;I would prefer you find a non-lethal way to solve your argument&quot;, and it was really not easy for them to grasp this.)<br /> <br /> So I think very clear reminder of the &quot;Orichalcum rule&quot; or whatever it is called in a game is a very good thing. It helps remind the purpose of the game for the party.<br /> <br /> To come back to the thread, I houserule many Charms in the following area :<br /> <br /> Instead of repurchase of Charms, I usually prefer having to complete some kind of quest or success to unlock it. Lots of repurchases are really not fun for the players.<br /> <br /> Lots of Charms are offered in a package, like the Charms from Craft, that I fond very boring to buy 1 by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T05:38:57-08:00","id":1362858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362856#post1362856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think very clear reminder of the &quot;Orichalcum rule&quot; or whatever it is called in a game is a very good thing. It helps remind the purpose of the game for the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, I think a reminder of that rule is good to have, but do we really need to have it told to us three times (two of which could have been word count used for other things we did not get)?<br /> <br /> And also to get back on topic:<br /> <br /> We have a tiered system for Craft in our games. If you just want to craft just one thing, like swords then you follow the rules as written. If you want to be a more general crafter you can pick something more encompassing for x2 cost per dot. If you want to be the omni-crafter you can take Craft: All for x3 cost. This rule came about because Craft tends to be enough of an XP sink as is considering the bloat of its charm tree.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25108-ikeulhu","name":"ikeulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:37:08-08:00","id":1362871,"title":"","content":"Retroactive Dragon Experience.<br /> <br /> So no character can have more than (Sessions played \u00d74) Dragon Experience. But sometimes you just can't shoehorn an Aspect bonus in, and other times you might hit every point in the Aspect box, and play up the Great Curse and cede a scene. So if you don't earn the full amount of Dragon Experience one session, you can make it up at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> This is especially noted for Air Aspects who get DX for achieving long term plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T09:53:53-08:00","id":1362905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362846#post1362846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general rules of a game serve as the common framework for the players and GM to communicate their story with and those three rules break that understanding, communication, and trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha? I think the last time I used the Orichalcum Rule as a GM was to allow a character to pick a lock with some improvised scraps of metal that were laying around. By the rules of DnD you NEED the item set called \u201cThieves\u2019 Tools\u201d to be able to attempt to pick a lock. The last time I ruled against a player with the orichalcum rule it\u2019s because he had a setup where he couldn\u2019t die except in incredibly specific and hard to engineer circumstances, which made the rest of the party feel like utterly useless chumps and was ruining their fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362871#post1362871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Retroactive Dragon Experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a great idea. Sometimes you end the session JUST before one of the players was about to get their xp, or gets it just barely twice in a session and it sucks otherwise. Especially if the session focuses more on an element of one characters backstory or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T10:11:18-08:00","id":1362909,"title":"","content":"I'm going to point out that Hark has been banned, so there's not much point addressing your points about the Orichalcum Rule to him.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see the idea of the retroactive Dragon Experience, but tbh, I find it quite difficult to decide how much Lunar XP my players should get after the session, but the fact that sometimes I'm not sure if they ought to get their Role Bonus, but they definitely get the bonus for ceding the scene, makes it much easier to decide! So I don't really want to have to remember for later sessions (it'd involve a lot of notes).<br /> (I do tend to err slightly on the side of &quot;yes&quot; for whether to give the bonuses to the players who've got less Lunar xp previously than the others though)<br /> <br /> I'm generally happy with the amount they get (about 2 per session per player on average, though of course it goes up and down). That is a decent idea for an ST who wanted to increase the average<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T11:32:11-08:00","id":1362921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362909#post1362909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to point out that Hark has been banned, so there's not much point addressing your points about the Orichalcum Rule to him.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see the idea of the retroactive Dragon Experience, but tbh, I find it quite difficult to decide how much Lunar XP my players should get after the session, but the fact that sometimes I'm not sure if they ought to get their Role Bonus, but they definitely get the bonus for ceding the scene, makes it much easier to decide! So I don't really want to have to remember for later sessions (it'd involve a lot of notes).<br /> (I do tend to err slightly on the side of &quot;yes&quot; for whether to give the bonuses to the players who've got less Lunar xp previously than the others though)<br /> <br /> I'm generally happy with the amount they get (about 2 per session per player on average, though of course it goes up and down). That is a decent idea for an ST who wanted to increase the average</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually give the full Solar/DB/whatev exp except when the players as a group really played poorly and were of bad faith and put a bad mood. I have seen only rares situation where my players felt motivated to &quot;play better&quot; because I didn't award bonus experience in game. I'm interested in having the opinion of you people about this topic, maybe you can open my mind to new ideas. <br /> <br /> Quick question, because I don't want to do the same mistake : What is the exact rule for moderation ? Do not talk after being moderated I guess ? I'm asking this but I guess I'll go find out the rules myself after this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T12:56:54-08:00","id":1362939,"title":"","content":"Retroactive splat exp is a pretty neat idea, I like that.<br /> <br /> In my casual group I just straight up award splat exp at 50% the rate of normal exp (so 2.5 per game). The group has very little time to learn and get better at the rules, so trying to explain and enforce the requirements for splat exp would just take away from the game rather than add to it. Plus at the end of the day it's mostly me spending the exp on their Sheet, so it wouldn't really work as an incentive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362921#post1362921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, because I don't want to do the same mistake : What is the exact rule for moderation ? Do not talk after being moderated I guess ? I'm asking this but I guess I'll go find out the rules myself after this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a standard rule on forums that you don't disrupt threads by arguing about a mod ruling in it, and I assume that goes double when your moderation is literally &quot;don't post here anymore&quot;. If Hark wanted to make a case to Lioness that he wasn't being disruptive he could've taken it to PMs, but instead he chose to just completely disregard the moderation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T14:05:43-08:00","id":1362949,"title":"","content":"I don't want to stick on this too much, and hopefully the mods don't mind me answering things that are more their baliwick, but this is from the second paragraph of the Forum Rules post:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Disputes between community members and the moderators, web administrators or Onyx Path staff should be handled privately, as should discussion of site policy and moderator actions.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So, arguing a mod ruling in-thread is formally against the rules, not just a matter of forum culture.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> And to get in topic:<br /> <br /> Doing it from 2e I forgot to add my voice to all of the people that just use XP instead of BP at character creation, and use flat costs for everything. We also generally ignore training times... just makes all that easier.<br /> <br /> Something that's not quite a full house rule, because it's still in flux: When using the full sail rules, PCs and major NPCs all get one action before the captain of their ship makes a roll. The goal is to make sure people without Sail and their own boat do things besides wait for a boarding action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T14:36:23-08:00","id":1362956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362921#post1362921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually give the full Solar/DB/whatev exp except when the players as a group really played poorly and were of bad faith and put a bad mood. I have seen only rares situation where my players felt motivated to &quot;play better&quot; because I didn't award bonus experience in game. I'm interested in having the opinion of you people about this topic, maybe you can open my mind to new ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the role xp for ceding the scene <i>might </i>help ensure some players don't feel their character is being constantly overshadowed by more talkative and active players. I didn't use to use Solar XP, but my friend said he found it useful for that, so I use Lunar XP now for my current game. Of course, while I think generally speaking they do cede the scene to the appropriate person, they're E2 rather than 5, so their powers are more niche, and also the group is much better at sticking together than my previous game, so are more likely to have the opportunity to say &quot;I'm going to step back and let X handle it.&quot; Essentially, I'd need a control group to be sure.<br /> But I think this works.<br /> <br /> The other stuff... eh, no I don't think it really makes much difference. The role bonuses are irrelevant about 75% of the time because they already got the XP for ceding the scene some time during the game.<br /> In the first few games, they got quite a bit for revealing stuff about the character, but now they've mostly... well, revealed them. I also found a lot of the PCs have Major intimacies that they don't really bring up, so don't get Lunar XP for... I guess if they wanted they could, but they seem happy with things as they are, I guess. Most sessions everyone who was there gets at least 2, and a couple get 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to XP encouraging roleplaying in certain ways, I think it depends a lot on the players honestly.<br /> Oh, it also depends on the Caste, and how their character relates to that caste. More traditional takes on Castes tend to do better than unusual takes on them. Which I don't like, but plenty of people would be happy with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-23-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T14:54:25-08:00","id":1362961,"title":"","content":"Just remembered one:<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgical rituals can be purchased at character creation in place of merits (on a dot-for-dot basis) or for 1 BP per dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T15:38:12-08:00","id":1362970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362909#post1362909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the idea of the retroactive Dragon Experience, but tbh, I find it quite difficult to decide how much Lunar XP my players should get after the session, but the fact that sometimes I'm not sure if they ought to get their Role Bonus, but they definitely get the bonus for ceding the scene, makes it much easier to decide! So I don't really want to have to remember for later sessions (it'd involve a lot of notes).<br /> (I do tend to err slightly on the side of &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; for whether to give the bonuses to the players who've got less Lunar xp previously than the others though)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for reference: because I'm a massive nerd, I do know what DX my players miss out on each session (it's always Aspect, Expression is pretty easy to hit).<br /> <br /> But I don't really care? So long as they don't end up with more than (Sessions \u00d74) Dragon Experience then it all works out in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T20:31:49-08:00","id":1363000,"title":"","content":"XP-wise, I have taken up a prior ST's ruling: Everyone gets 4 Splat XP per session, and then the ST asks the players to nominate a MVP among them to receive one extra Splat XP. The variation per player tends to be pretty small and as players I've seen us sort of vaguely self-regulate when we're teetering between two choices, like &quot;oh, I got it last time and I really liked that stunt you did, I vote you get the MVP point&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T00:14:18-08:00","id":1363028,"title":"","content":"Some simpler surface-level ones that I do:<br /> <br /> Flat XP (though I actually don't mind bp too much, so don't worry on that).<br /> <br /> Having a Langauge Merit doesn't 100% gurantee you speak every language in that Direction. You still more or less can communicate, but depending on how faraway you are, there's a bit of a &quot;learning time&quot; based on some amount of scenes before you can speak. Kirighasti Flametongue to Yangese is probably a scene or two. City of the Steel Lotus might take four or five before you really got a hang of it. Basically folks can Conan-osmosis thier way through a langauage, but I tend to try to encourage a bit more on the differences to make Creaiton feel bigger. (Inspired a bit by Eric Minton's blog post <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2014/08/25/exalted-language-families-and-dialects/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.)<br /> <br /> Mighty Thews Merit is two-dots and just gives two dice instead of scaling, as it kind fo makes it screwy as a Merit otherwise.<br /> <br /> I ignore the off-hand penalty and the one-dot version of Ambidextrolus entirely.<br /> <br /> I have some tweaks to dice roll stuff. Mainly some alternate Attributes to make Dexterity and Wits a bit less dominating (I just kind of just assume the Lunar Charms get repalced or deleted in sucha cotnext), plus Abilities in some social contexts or Introduce Fact stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T00:21:13-08:00","id":1363029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ikeulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1362858#post1362858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely, I think a reminder of that rule is good to have, but do we really need to have it told to us three times (two of which could have been word count used for other things we did not get)?<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually do think they're kind of distinct if you think context of WW games in general. They always list the Golden Rule (you can change things). That I think is different from the Oricalchum Rule in the sense that it points out &quot;Games aren't physics here&quot; thing. This is kind of a response mostly to how a lot of late 2e went more than anything, where folks got in their heads the mechanics were a physics simulator. It is kind of helpful to be upfront on that. Or the common bits i have seen where &quot;If we assume the mechanics are true, then the setting is wrong.&quot; It's basically a resposne to that.<br /> <br /> I kinda thing the Storyteller rule fits in that a bit, but it's more a referree rule than the other two. Golden again is &quot;You can change.&quot; Oricalchum is &quot;The mechanics aren't physics.&quot; And Storyteller is there to basically say &quot;RAI beats RAW&quot;, which is different again there. They might be able to be consolidated, but I think that they also show up in the Storypath games by OPP to me indicates that they're not a bad set. It's just that before Exalted 3e, WW/OPP games were explicit about GR, but not the other two.<br /> <br /> (Red Rule should have been here instead of social stuff, but later games have takent hat into account too.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T00:44:39-08:00","id":1363033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363028#post1363028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some tweaks to dice roll stuff. Mainly some alternate Attributes to make Dexterity and Wits a bit less dominating (I just kind of just assume the Lunar Charms get repalced or deleted in sucha cotnext), plus Abilities in some social contexts or Introduce Fact stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind giving them ? I'm interested","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T01:57:50-08:00","id":1363045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363033#post1363033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you mind giving them ? I'm interested</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally taken from Everspace on the Discord and modified for my doc as follows: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Action</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Dice Pool</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Disengage</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dexterity + (Althetics or Dodge)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Join Battle</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Perception or Wits) + Awareness</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Parry</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Dexterity or Stamina) + (Weapon Skill or Resistance)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Read Intentions</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Perception or Wits) + (Investigation or Socialize or Non-Standard Ability)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Resolve</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Charisma or Wits) + Integrity</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Rush</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Dexterity or Strength) + Athletics</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> The Introduce Fact stuff is not quite as thought-out yet and something I wanna go through the Charms related to already to be sure what of htem need worke don.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T02:51:40-08:00","id":1363048,"title":"","content":"I like this. Can each player chose which stats he uses ? Or do you fix the given attribute for everyone once and for all ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T03:36:44-08:00","id":1363050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363048#post1363048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. Can each player chose which stats he uses ? Or do you fix the given attribute for everyone once and for all ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're just alt options to build the pool. It's up to players to decide how they pick which.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T05:57:17-08:00","id":1363062,"title":"","content":"I've reduced Solar XP to 1 XP per &quot;instance&quot; but instead of just applying to an individual character the XP is given to every characte. It's still capped at 4 / Session.<br /> This means that if there's a social heavy game the Dawn doesn't get penalized for not finding something to punch or the other way around.<br /> <br /> I'm also using alternative crafting rules and, should it ever come up, an alternative bureaucracy system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11711-musclewizard","name":"Musclewizard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T06:26:43-08:00","id":1363065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363050#post1363050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're just alt options to build the pool. It's up to players to decide how they pick which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it chosen freely by the player or decided by ST based on the context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T06:36:05-08:00","id":1363067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363045#post1363045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Originally taken from Everspace on the Discord and modified for my doc as follows: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Action</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Dice Pool</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Disengage</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dexterity + (Althetics or Dodge)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Join Battle</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Perception or Wits) + Awareness</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Parry</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Dexterity or Stamina) + (Weapon Skill or Resistance)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Read Intentions</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Perception or Wits) + (Investigation or Socialize or Non-Standard Ability)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Resolve</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Charisma or Wits) + Integrity</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Rush</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">(Dexterity or Strength) + Athletics</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> The Introduce Fact stuff is not quite as thought-out yet and something I wanna go through the Charms related to already to be sure what of htem need worke don.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has potential. I'm a little concerned that Wits and Perception seem to be bleeding into each other but aside from that it's pretty logical.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T07:46:26-08:00","id":1363074,"title":"","content":"Well, in our game every player has the option to receive an additional <i><b>2 [Splat] xp</b></i> per session for providing a Journal entry or Article of World Building. There has never been a specific amount of word count required, but I always shoot for 1500+ words, though I often go well beyond a 2k word count. . In my opinion, it helps to bring the characters alive, fix the narrative in the minds of players (and characters), and move the narrative forward. But then, I have always been a huge fan of Blue-Booking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:07:35-08:00","id":1363077,"title":"","content":"Is it me or most house rules are about the craft system and the exp system ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:23:46-08:00","id":1363082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363077#post1363077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or most house rules are about the craft system and the exp system ?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, both of those systems are ones where people can tweak things without a bunch of immediate implosions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T08:58:15-08:00","id":1363091,"title":"","content":"Exp makes perfect sense to me. I've been runnning my game for almost 12 years and recognise my requirements there are pretty different to those of most people in this thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:11:15-08:00","id":1363097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363082#post1363082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, both of those systems are ones where people can tweak things without a bunch of immediate implosions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess ... that makes sense. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have a simple house rule for exp cost in order for them to not be totally unbalanced compared to chargen ? I think the main thing I want is linear cost in Abilities/attributes. <br /> <br /> For the moment I'm with something very simple like : 5 pex (-1 favored) for each Ability level, 10 pex for each Attribute level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T09:51:00-08:00","id":1363106,"title":"","content":"The system I use (credit to Dankmuffins) is basically... <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Attribute Increase</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9xp per dot (7xp Caste/Favored)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ability Increase</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4xp per dot (3xp Caste/Favored)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Specialty</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Purchased Merit</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3xp per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Willpower</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8xp per dot</td> </tr> </table></div> The cost of Charms, Martial Arts Charms, Spells, and Evocations is unchanged. Casteless Lunars still get their cost discount for increasing unfavored Attributes (8xp) and buying unfavored Charms (9xp).<br /> Remove BP, instead replacing it with a pool of &quot;starting XP&quot; that is spent in place of BP. This is calculated by multiplying the normal BP allotment by 3, so standard Solars and Lunars get 45 and standard Deebs get 54. As stated earlier, if you have leftover &quot;starting XP&quot; (and given the way the costs work, it's very possible for you to have 1-2 of it hanging around), it is converted to splat XP, so you don't miss out on anything by not spending every last point.<br /> <br /> While I'm sure there's imperfections, I haven't yet found an issue with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:12:23-08:00","id":1363109,"title":"","content":"That seems fine to me. Why not use the BP since the cost are unified, except for the freebies maybe ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:17:33-08:00","id":1363111,"title":"","content":"BP costs are deliberately designed to encourage Abilities and discourage Charms. So with BP costs people would probably buy less charms and more abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T10:34:17-08:00","id":1363117,"title":"","content":"I guess at this point I could arbitrarily distribute 1 more attribute point, 4 Abilities points and 1 Charm and be done with it. I'll see depending if my group is mechanically saavy or not I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:15:58-08:00","id":1363144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363065#post1363065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it chosen freely by the player or decided by ST based on the context?</div> </div> </div> </div>Player. Just like they choose whether htey're using Charisma or Appearance when leading troops. Unless they stunt it it's mechancially the same.<br /> <br /> I forgot to add, but (Strength or Dexteirty) + (Weapon Ability) for heavy and unarmed hand-to-hand attacks was also something else I'm weighing on. It's also something Lunars have just a Charm for but It hink would not hurt anything if it were the baseline as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 01-24-2020, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:22:34-08:00","id":1363147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363077#post1363077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or most house rules are about the craft system and the exp system ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually use Craft more-or-less as written. The only things I've considered is 1) Getting rid of basic slots and 2) I make it so that anyone can downgrade white points to gold points isnce they're not very useful for not-Exalts or most games. I think the Solar Charmset is more a culprit to Craft's woes than Craft itself, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:23:51-08:00","id":1363149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363067#post1363067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has potential. I'm a little concerned that Wits and Perception seem to be bleeding into each other but aside from that it's pretty logical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think generally it's fine since I like having flexibility primarily. So while there's soem bleed, I don't think that's a problem if it encourages diversity in build.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:44:03-08:00","id":1363154,"title":"","content":"On the whole XP and Craft thing:<br /> <br /> For XP, it seems worth remembering that XP might be the most house ruled thing in all of Exalted. Discussions about merging BP and XP in various forms have been around since 1e. As something that's endured for three editions, for people that aren't just scrapping standard Exalted system for something else, it's got the weight of time on it's &quot;side.&quot;<br /> <br /> For crafting... well... it's been a fairly contentious thing for 3e. Even for people that generally like the base-line system, it's got some warts on it (made worse by the Solar Craft Charms). And as noted, also like my Sail house rule, it's fairly contained system so it's easy to find a fix that works for you and get to the game.<br /> <br /> I know there are a lot of us that want to rework how equipment Tags work (esp. after the release of Scion 2e and Trinity 2e and how weapons and armor got handled there), but mucking with combat takes a lot of time to fine tune that sort of change. I certainly haven't settled on a version of it I'm happy with yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:12:10-08:00","id":1363188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363147#post1363147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually use Craft more-or-less as written. The only things I've considered is 1) Getting rid of basic slots and 2) I make it so that anyone can downgrade white points to gold points since they're not very useful for not-Exalts or most games. I think the Solar Charmset is more a culprit to Craft's woes than Craft itself, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed... We use Craft as written... I actually really enjoy the Craft System a lot, and I use it extensively... This without having a single Craft Charm as a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:59:36-08:00","id":1363201,"title":"","content":"1) Ties break in the favour of the player if the stunt is equal.<br /> 2) Free alternating -1 and -2 HL every 50 earned XP (because I find buying HLs boring)<br /> 3) You can spend your WP after the roll as a player, I can\u2019t as the ST.<br /> 4) I have some rules about not stacking Charm buys too high in One Ability/Attribute (which except the Supernal Ability for Solars)<br /> 5) I\u2019ve slightly changed some of the extended action rules that mean that failing at something big tends to Have Giant Consequences instead of potentially Just Failing.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main thing I really want to try to houserule well is Helping rules that I can use generically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","name":"Whybover","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T11:02:30-08:00","id":1363655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use#post1362488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the impression, that this topic was already somewhere in the forum, but now I cannot find it (If I was right, feel free to delete or merge it).<br /> <br /> Tell me about you houserules. Especially the smaller ones, one so minuscule that you wouldn't bother mentioning it in other threads. Why you introduced them? Do they fix something you find a bug or do they intentionally change the tone or scope of the game. You can list just some of them which work particularly well.<br /> <br /> This is a [+] thread, notation borrowed from another forum, so we generally simply do not criticise other's solutions. What we might do is to suggest some different modifications to the same effect. We may ask one another about the practical effects of the changes etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I let players call out examples of good roleplaying and give each other a little bonus xp because of it, in general I am more liberal with xp because I like higher powered games, I also give more dots more bonus points for character generation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T12:15:21-08:00","id":1363662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363091#post1363091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exp makes perfect sense to me. I've been runnning my game for almost 12 years and recognise my requirements there are pretty different to those of most people in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I used to run a Solar game, I didn't give out Solar XP except at the end of stories occasionally. Which sounds awful to some people probably, but that game is now at 485xp+50 Solar xp.<br /> <br /> Such long-running games are very different from a new game, where giving out 9xp (5xp+4 Solar/etc) a session can work fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T19:06:54-08:00","id":1363893,"title":"","content":"Remembered another: Purchased merits are a flat 3 XP per dot, to avoid the weirdness of Mighty Thew 3 costing twice as much as Fleet of Foot (not to mention way too much in general).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T21:55:17-08:00","id":1363909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363893#post1363893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remembered another: Purchased merits are a flat 3 XP per dot, to avoid the weirdness of Mighty Thew 3 costing twice as much as Fleet of Foot (not to mention way too much in general).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is acutally why I made Mighty Thews a flat 2-dot Merit since it seems actually kind of aberrant in that context of things, since Merits are by default flat anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T22:48:10-08:00","id":1363918,"title":"","content":"In my game we just stuck with me giving out small allotments of BP rather than XP. BPs make creating new characters a lot more fun and intuitive for new players, and honestly it worked fine for a 1 year campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T11:29:00-08:00","id":1363997,"title":"","content":"Character Generation:<br /> <br /> <br /> I also use XP instead of BP, at all levels:<br /> <br /> 80/52/40 xp split for Attributes<br /> 84xp for Abilities<br /> 39xp for Merits @ 3xp per dot<br /> 150 xp for charms<br /> 100 Bonus XP<br /> <br /> It allows for slightly stronger starting characters with <br /> a bit more breadth and depth.<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> For many charms, if the resolution is too complex, I simplify it to something quick and easy to remember.<br /> <br /> EXP Awards:<br /> <br /> I'm very generous with XP, as it seems PCs never have enough <br /> to actually fulfill their character builds. <br /> <br /> Essence:<br /> <br /> I've stretched out the Essence per XP ratio <br /> as a result of a more generous XP award system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T13:55:39-08:00","id":1364029,"title":"","content":"New Characters Joining a Campaign:<br /> <br /> Inspired by the (unforgivably terrible) 1st Edition rule (which is new characters get ~55% of base XP with no story awards), new characters joining a campaign get full XP as if they'd been in play from the start, but no Solar XP (subject to my previous house rule about being able to make-up any Solar XP missed out on).<br /> <br /> New characters can bypass this and start with full Solar XP, if they take over play of an established NPC, already in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T16:49:09-08:00","id":1364065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1364029#post1364029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Characters Joining a Campaign:<br /> <br /> Inspired by the (unforgivably terrible) 1st Edition rule (which is new characters get ~55% of base XP with no story awards), new characters joining a campaign get full XP as if they'd been in play from the start, but no Solar XP (subject to my previous house rule about being able to make-up any Solar XP missed out on).<br /> <br /> New characters can bypass this and start with full Solar XP, if they take over play of an established NPC, already in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>How have the players of new characters taken that rule? <br /> Have you had anyone opt to start with 0 splat XP? How many sesions in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:29:37-08:00","id":1364179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1364065#post1364065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How have the players of new characters taken that rule? <br /> Have you had anyone opt to start with 0 splat XP? How many sesions in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had one player join 8 sessions in who opted to take over an NPC. She seems happy with it, but also hasn't played Exalted since 1E and wanted me to make her character anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T16:35:39-08:00","id":1364431,"title":"","content":"Huh! Just put my current blend together.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> All rules related to First Age Artifice are cut. Relevant artifacts are treated just as any other artifact, though some will need maintenance occasionally. (This is unrolled, but will require tools and resources) Craft is one ability: like Lore, your background determines what you can do with it. Craft XP, slots and all associated rules are retained, but the project definitions are altered somewhat.<br /> <br /> Minor projects represent any craft based action that can be done immediately or in the short term, including appraisal or repair (now weighted as a full project). Major projects still include long term/large scale mortal craft usage, such as a banquet or a large supply of weapons/armor, but also include the construction of two dot artifacts: these require an extended roll as per superior projects. For all project levels but Legendary, you only need to spend XP for the first roll..<br /> <br /> Time to craft artifacts is judged ad hoc, and your base target numbers are 15 for a 2 dot artifact, 30 for a 3 dot, 50 for a 4 dot and 75 for a 5 dot. N/A remains at 200. The difficulty of the roll is determined by the finesse system from Sorcerous Workings<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts and Brawl are reunified: refer to the ability as Martial Arts and you do not need the merit to access it: your rating allows access to any style you can find a tutor for in story. The canonical Brawl charmset represents a character\u2019s natural techniques, and can be combined freely with the charms of other styles. However, Evocations may not be used in the same instant as Martial Arts charms, barring existing charm specific exemptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Artifact weaponry can combine traits (and thus tags) from multiple weapons. Generally this represents a weapon with multiple \u2018modes\u2019 such as the classic gunblade. All such combi-weapons are provisionally okayed by me, but their dual nature means combining multiple martial arts through them is something I\u2019d like to be consulted on first.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy operates on 2E principles of being understandable, codifiable and repeatable by trained mortals. Shamans and astrologers are usually Thaumaturgists, and a fair few sorcerers know a little of the arts too, since the knowledge overlaps with their studies. Thaumaturgy is divided into a set of special merits called Arts: each art runs from 1-3 dots, taking that Merit will allow you to use all rituals of the art through that degree. (There are some thaumaturgical rites that are 0 degree, any character can attempt these with an Occult roll) This goes against some of the design intent in 2E, but is a lot simpler than trying to cost out individual rituals. <br /> <br /> All other Thaumaturgical rules will be implemented as per 2E standard to begin with: if someone goes this route, I\u2019ll be looking to see how it does and will make adjustments IC if balance becomes a concern. For anyone without access to 2E the arts are as follows. If any of these interest you, PM me and I\u2019ll be happy to provide you with further information about exactly what Thaumaturgy can let you do with that ability.<ul><li>Alchemy,</li> <li>Astrology,</li> <li>Art of the Dead,</li> <li>Demon Summoning,</li> <li>Elemental Summoning,</li> <li>Enchantment,</li> <li>Geomancy,</li> <li>Husbandry,</li> <li>Spirit Beckoning,</li> <li>Warding and Exorcism,</li> <li>Weather Working.</li> </ul><br /> </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4086,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","user":"Croakamancer","date":". 01-31-2020, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T07:47:35-08:00","id":1366321,"title":"","content":"No Training Times, no Solar XP. Everyone gets 10xp per session and 30-50xp on completion of the Story Arc (5ish sessions). <br /> <br /> New characters start at 0 xp but earn triple xp per session until they're halfish way there, and double xp until they catch up. We got this way because the new players felt that making a character and then spending 100 xp was overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T07:59:35-08:00","id":1366324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1364029#post1364029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">new characters joining a campaign get full XP as if they'd been in play from the start, but no Solar XP</div> </div> </div> </div>I do the same. They also don't get Solar (well, in this game's case Lunar) XP if they miss a session.<br /> <br /> But when adjudicating Lunar XP awards, I do go a little softer on the people who are way behind: one player missed like 7 sessions in a row, another came in after maybe 5 or 6 sessions when his previous character died.<br /> <br /> I think it's worked fine. I should note that none of my players are playing sorcerers, Martial Artists, or buying evocations though. So everyone actually has pretty much the same amount of charms, it's just some characters have the odd extra dot in low-level secondary Abilities, rounding them out slightly.<br /> <br /> I feel this discourages players to not care if their character dies as they can just make a new one, but at the same time doesn't screw new characters. (I played a game once, Qin, where me and another guy went through 4-5 characters while a couple of other players kept the same one. Because our characters had so much less XP, combats were deadly for us while they were easy for the experienced guys.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T21:39:28-08:00","id":1369281,"title":"","content":"Couple other little ones about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> I straight-up got rid of off-hand penalties. It's a bit of minutia I don' tthink serves the system well at all. This also results in the one-dot version fo Ambidexterous being deleted since well, it don't do anything.<br /> <br /> Heavy weapons have no Defense penalty and Overwelming 2, since I don't see a reason for the former and i there's nothing in the system really taking advantage of the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:39:28-08:00","id":1369404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1369281#post1369281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy weapons have no Defense penalty and Overwelming 2, since I don't see a reason for the former and i there's nothing in the system really taking advantage of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that, mundane heavy weapons need a little extra help and more overwhelming is an important benefit enjoyed by their artifact equivilents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T21:49:09-07:00","id":1375545,"title":"","content":"I allow sorcerers who do workings to count the xp spent working an effect towards the spellification of that effect (to avoid xp anxiety around workings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T01:50:35-07:00","id":1375562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375545#post1375545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I allow sorcerers who do workings to count the xp spent working an effect towards the spellification of that effect (to avoid xp anxiety around workings).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I didn't understand your post. Could you rephrase or give an example ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T02:08:05-07:00","id":1375567,"title":"","content":"Sure. My sorcerer player wanted a grenade (glass potion) version of Mists of Eventide, as they were planning on a heist. They had several days to prepare, and the sorcerer did not know the spell 'Mists of Eventide'. I allowed the grenade to be prepared as a working (costing the xp).<br /> <br /> Later, after the heist, the sorcerer was impressed enough with the results that they wanted to have the effect more 'on-hand', so they paid to buy 'Mists of Eventide' the spell and waited the training time. But I did not charge the full xp price! I only charged the difference between the listed price on page 177 minus the xp they'd spent so far doing workings for the effect of 'Mists of Eventide'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T02:30:48-07:00","id":1375569,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah sure that makes sense and it avoids paying a full price for something you already used","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T06:12:01-07:00","id":1375589,"title":"","content":"The most important:<br /> Splat XP has a Maximum of 1/player BUT all players gain the xp. So if the dawn ceded the scene, the twilight, eclipse and zenith hit their role bonus then all players get 4 splat xp.<br /> Others:<br /> A craft re-write<br /> (usually) training times are ignored entirely<br /> The lose a limb option is not 1/story. (We have had someone who had to lose 3 limbs to survive and it turned into a decent RP moment)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T15:24:47-07:00","id":1375867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whybover</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1363201#post1363201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Free alternating -1 and -2 HL every 50 earned XP (because I find buying HLs boring)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that in addition to allowing the purchase of Ox-Body technique, or do you remove that charm from the game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) I have some rules about not stacking Charm buys too high in One Ability/Attribute (which except the Supernal Ability for Solars) </div> </div> </div>Could I ask you to elaborate on those rules? What kind of limits do you set?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T20:01:41-07:00","id":1375891,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s one I just came up with this morning:<br /> <br /> <b>Rotating Volleys:</b> A battle group can ignore the Slow tag by reducing its Size bonus to attack and damage rolls by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T02:09:23-07:00","id":1375913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375867#post1375867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that in addition to allowing the purchase of Ox-Body technique, or do you remove that charm from the game?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Could I ask you to elaborate on those rules? What kind of limits do you set?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would ditch the Charm if you're doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T04:31:16-07:00","id":1375931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375913#post1375913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would ditch the Charm if you're doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. Having like 10 hp at 150 exp seems kinda low","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T06:55:05-07:00","id":1375953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375931#post1375931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure. Having like 10 hp at 150 exp seems kinda low</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd tie it to Essence, so that you get Essence x Ox-Body Technique for free. I take your point that 10 HLs isn't a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:08:59-07:00","id":1375959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375953#post1375953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd tie it to Essence, so that you get Essence x Ox-Body Technique for free. I take your point that 10 HLs isn't a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mention it but that's one of my Houserule : You get (Essence) Ox-Body technique for free, you can pay more if you want. This way I don't feel bad having some strong NPC's because they won't one shot the bureaucratic nerd guy that didn't invest a lot in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T12:11:11-07:00","id":1375993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375959#post1375959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mention it but that's one of my Houserule : You get (Essence) Ox-Body technique for free, you can pay more if you want. This way I don't feel bad having some strong NPC's because they won't one shot the bureaucratic nerd guy that didn't invest a lot in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even a nerdy demigod is a demigod, so this works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T17:48:41-07:00","id":1376042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1375959#post1375959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mention it but that's one of my Houserule : You get (Essence) Ox-Body technique for free, you can pay more if you want. This way I don't feel bad having some strong NPC's because they won't one shot the bureaucratic nerd guy that didn't invest a lot in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You as a player are already in control over whether an attack is withering or decisive, and absent piling on numerous attack Charms, it's pretty easy to have a good idea of how much damage a decisive attack is going to do. If you the ST don't want an NPC to one-shot the weedy demigod, don't throw a decisive attack at him while the NPC has 7+ Initiative.<br /> <br /> (I have an example of this from my most recent game session. The ST threw a noodle-armed Abyssal necromancer at us; my character, Knight Raiton, had 21 Initiative, but didn't want to kill her - for one, his fighting style is fairly nonlethal, but also, Lyse wanted to add the necromancer's form to her library of Stolen Faces, so she needed to be the one to secure the kill. So when Knight Raiton's turn came up, he grappled the Abyssal instead.)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, since only PCs are guaranteed to use the XP system, how do you determine NPCs' health?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T02:59:02-07:00","id":1376091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1376042#post1376042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You as a player are already in control over whether an attack is withering or decisive, and absent piling on numerous attack Charms, it's pretty easy to have a good idea of how much damage a decisive attack is going to do. If you the ST don't want an NPC to one-shot the weedy demigod, don't throw a decisive attack at him while the NPC has 7+ Initiative.<br /> <br /> (I have an example of this from my most recent game session. The ST threw a noodle-armed Abyssal necromancer at us; my character, Knight Raiton, had 21 Initiative, but didn't want to kill her - for one, his fighting style is fairly nonlethal, but also, Lyse wanted to add the necromancer's form to her library of Stolen Faces, so she needed to be the one to secure the kill. So when Knight Raiton's turn came up, he grappled the Abyssal instead.)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, since only PCs are guaranteed to use the XP system, how do you determine NPCs' health?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering in 2 parts : <br /> <br /> 1) To a certain extent, I don't like too much to treat a player character like &quot;I know you are weak so I'm going to be kinder with you&quot;. I, of course, do it all the time depending on the circumstances, but I feel there is more tension if the players don't think I'm just going to be nicer with them. I had overall better results at the table by being more direct on these kind of things, as it had make many situations more deadly and the players felt more the tension, and played accordingly to the stakes I tried to give them.<br /> <br /> 2) I guess no one reads them (and it's fine, I don't either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), but I have a little home-brew in my signature where I recap of all the pools I expect to use for the NPC's. So I mainly use them in order to determine the NPC's stats, instead of using a character sheet and &quot;doing it like a PC&quot; (which is a design method I really dislike). If I described a rather weak non combattant Exalted, he will most likely be between 7 and 12 health, if it's an Exalted from a War-God I expect to fight well enough he will most likely have around 17 hp, etc ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T21:49:18-07:00","id":1376211,"title":"","content":"Just remembered one: Instead of requiring you to not win Join Battle to work, Open Palm Caress supersedes the normal cost of delaying your first action (and requires you to do so if you won Join Battle). Because right now it's the only Charm in the game that wants you to have <i>fewer</i> dice in the action it enhances, and that's terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T23:01:14-07:00","id":1376214,"title":"","content":"Players can speak in their human languages while in animal form for free. If the creature in question does not have vocal cords. They can spend a single mote to do it anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26022-miraclegrow","name":"MiracleGrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T02:30:59-07:00","id":1376227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362488-what-house-rules-do-you-use?p=1376211#post1376211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remembered one: Instead of requiring you to not win Join Battle to work, Open Palm Caress supersedes the normal cost of delaying your first action (and requires you to do so if you won Join Battle). Because right now it's the only Charm in the game that wants you to have <i>fewer</i> dice in the action it enhances, and that's terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>ACKCHYUALLY ...<br /> <br /> Brass Scales Falling p.292 of Exalted 3e Core requires to not use an excellency, but to roll a huge amount of 10 to be worth it. So it just sucks as much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T05:52:54-07:00","id":1376250,"title":"","content":"Brass Scales Falling is still better the more Attribute + Crafts you have. Open Palm Caress is <i>worse</i> the more Wits + Awareness you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member